      "writtenOn": "2020-04-30T16:41:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Presumably because of circular references. That is currently how it behaves so I wanted to make the behavior clear here.\n\nI spent a little time wondering how this would work for the other usages and it seems as though there are two separate categories:\n* If you specify sdk_version: \"none\" then \"none\" is used for all the stubs libraries. This is used for the ART APIs that have to bootstrap themselves up from nothing.\n* Otherwise, it uses \"current\" for \"public\" and \"system_current\" for \"system\" as described here. This is used for modules that provide public/test/system APIs but which do not themselves contribute to the main current/test_current/system_current APIs hence avoiding the cycle.\n\nIt looks as though we will need a way to provide per surface overrides of the sdk_version property.",
      "parentUuid": "e71f8342_ab9dc520",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "4f0cde0636909d3d58f35f60d6a64c826cd5109f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8eb7d934_38a2d648",
        "filename": "apex/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-30T16:54:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "- current usages of java_sdk_library don\u0027t contribute to the monolithic api surfaces so don\u0027t have to deal with the problems we have here. I think the way current users build makes sense, but it won\u0027t work for BCP libs\n- per-surface override.. hmm. I think perhaps what we need is just \"if sdk_version \u003d\u003d module_current, then use module_current for all the stubs too\". A little implicit, but it is kind of a special case.",
      "parentUuid": "38a86f86_69690ecf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 98,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "4f0cde0636909d3d58f35f60d6a64c826cd5109f",
